Description: autotests: Xwayland going away with its window selected
 The Xwayland crash test also checks that the compositor says no window is
 selected after the selected X11 window went with Xwayland. A new test,
 testTranslucencyXwayland, kills Xwayland with an X11 window selected, then
 selects two Wayland windows in turn under the translucency effect at the
 edition's Inactive=91: it fails on the effect's script error and on an
 opacity held below 100 % on the selected window (queue row 862).
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-needed, no contributions to KDE for now; the failure is kept in the edition's list of unfiled failures
Last-Update: 2026-11-24

